  Hmm.  On the other hand, one benefit of template metaprogramming is
the ability to reduce an entire problem down to one or two machine
instructions at runtime.  For an extreme example, see the Turing machines
done in template metaprogramming style; IIRC, you can type up a Turing
machine program in C++ and have it compile down to two instructions:
    LOAD <magicnumber>
    CALL PRINT_NUMBER
where <magicnumber> is the result of running the Turing machine program.
Sizewise bloat, bah.

